<title>FRANCE: Thomson-CSF unit wins ESA contract.</title>
<headline>Thomson-CSF unit wins ESA contract.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thomson-CSF Services &amp; Systemes Sol Spatiaux, a unit of Thomson-CSF, which is 58 percent held by state-owned Thomson SA, signed a ground control contract with the European Space Agency (ESA) for the Envisat-1 satellite.</p>
<p>Thomson-CSF said in a statement that it would manage the project, whose value is estimated at 450 million francs.</p>
<p>Envisat-1 is scheduled to be launched in 1999, replacing the ERS-1 and 2 satellites studying the earth's surface and atmosphere.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
